{\pard \qc \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs36 Findings Guide\par}
{\pard \qc \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0  Prof.\u160 ?Jack Reilly\par}
{\pard \qc \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0  F2026\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Each finding and the accompanying graph, source, and comment will have its own page in the report.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b General layout of a findings page}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 1.\tx360\tab Finding statement\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 2.\tx360\tab Graph\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 3.\tx360\tab Source\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 4.\tx360\tab Comment (if needed)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 5.\tx360\tab Page break\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Finding statement}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Your first finding statement will go two lines below the \u8220"FINDINGS\u8221" header.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Your finding statement should be numbered (for example, your fourth finding will start \u8220"4.\u8221").\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Do not include an indent anywhere in the finding statement.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Do not include (n=) at the end of your finding statement in the Findings section. This is because (n=) should be included in your graph.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab Note: you {\i will} include (n=) following your findings in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "executive-summary.qmd"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
Executive Summary
}}}
.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab See class slides for how to write finding statements.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Graph}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab You will copy and paste your graph below your finding statement.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Graphs should be made in Excel.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Follow the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "graphing.qmd"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
PST 315 Graphing Guidelines
}}}
!\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Your graph should be centered on the page.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Do not insert a screenshot of your graph.}\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Source}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Below your graph you will type the source of your graph directly into the Word document. The source should read something along the lines of: \u8220"Data collected by John Doe and analyzed by Jane Doe for XYZ Organization, Community Link Project, November 2025.\u8221"\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Comment}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Some graphs will require a comment typed into Word below the source. This includes aggregated graphs, open-ended response graphs, graphs where the percentages do not add up to 100%, and graphs where you group multiple responses into one category (including \u8220"other\u8221" categories).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Page break}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 To insert a new page, add a page break. {\b Do not add a section break.} Use Insert \u8594 ? Page Break, and begin your next finding at the start of the next page.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Example findings page\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li720 \fi0 {\b About this example}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li720 \fi0 This example uses {\b sample data}. Skills Win Coaching Organization is a real Syracuse University program, but the numbers shown are invented for teaching purposes and are not actual SWCO results.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The whole page \u8211- statement, graph, source, and comment \u8211- looks like this:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li1080 \fi-360 3.\tx360\tab 34% of respondents said more activities would improve the site sessions.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\pict\pngblip\picw1408\pich887\picwgoal10188\pichgoal6418 }\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Source:} Sample data collected and analyzed by Jordan Alvarez for the Skills Win Coaching Organization, Community Link Project, November 2026.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Comment:} Respondents could give only one answer, so percentages total 100%. Responses that named a specific activity were grouped into \u8220"More activities.\u8221"\par}
}
